From: Lenny Szabo
To: All
Subj: Zork I: your first ten minutes (no spoilers)
Date: 06-28-88 20:45

Zork I is up in the Games file area (get ZORK1.EXE AND the ZORK1.DAT
story file, the first is useless without the second).  For those of you
who have never played a text adventure, welcome to the best thing a
computer can do with no graphics at all.

You start West of House, in an open field, next to a white house with a
boarded front door and a small mailbox.  Your first ten minutes:

  * OPEN MAILBOX.  READ what you find.  It's polite.
  * Walk around the house.  Front doors are overrated.
  * EXAMINE everything.  TAKE anything that isn't nailed down.
  * INVENTORY (or just I) tells you what you're carrying.
  * Draw a map on paper.  Seriously.  Graph paper.  Arrows.

And the most important advice anybody will ever give you about Zork: if
the game says "It is pitch black.  You are likely to be eaten by a
grue," believe it.

Lenny
... I am in a maze of twisty little passages, all alike.
