From: Susan Oyelaran
To: All
Subj: RISC Dragon survival guide
Date: 11-10-89 21:30

After a month of being murdered by Stray Pointers, I have learned things.
I share them so that you may suffer less:

  1. BANK YOUR GOLD before going into the forest.  When you die, you
     lose what you're carrying.  The bank doesn't care that you died.
  2. Buy ARMOUR before weapons.  Nobody tells you this.  Doris's shop.
  3. Don't fight your master until the Training Hall says you're ready.
     You can't run from a master.  I tried.  He watched.
  4. The healer charges more at higher levels.  Keep enough gold on
     you to get patched up, and heal BEFORE the next fight, not after.
  5. Visit the Floating Point Inn.  Listen to the bartender.  Half the
     rumours are true.  The other half are funny.
  6. Gems are worth something at the Inn.  Don't sell them for gold.

Susan
... Slain by a Stray Pointer, 11 times and counting.
